{%- comment -%}
  The product breadcrumb, resolved once and rendered two ways, so the trail Google is
  shown and the trail a visitor can click cannot drift apart.

    {% render 'product-crumb', format: 'json', product: product, collection: collection %}
    {% render 'product-crumb', format: 'html', product: product, collection: collection %}

  Rung 2 used to point at /search?q=<type>. Google treats internal search results as low
  value, and the click sent shoppers to a slower, worse page than the category collection
  that already exists. The search URL survives only as a last resort, so a part whose type
  matches no category still gets a trail.

  Rung 2 names a CATEGORY, so it matches against the part-type collections by name rather
  than taking whatever product.collections happens to list first. A part is in its vehicle
  collections too — a Ford Ranger alternator is in "Used Ford Parts" and "Used Ford Ranger
  Parts" as well as "Electrical & Modules" — and "Home / Used Ford Parts / alternator" is
  the wrong trail: it says where the part came from, not what it is.

  The category list lives in the category-handles snippet, shared with /collections.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture category_handles -%}{%- render 'category-handles' -%}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- liquid
  assign categories = category_handles | strip | split: ','
  assign crumb_title = ''
  assign crumb_url = ''

  if collection and categories contains collection.handle
    assign crumb_title = collection.title
    assign crumb_url = collection.url
  else
    for c in product.collections
      if categories contains c.handle
        assign crumb_title = c.title
        assign crumb_url = c.url
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  if crumb_url == blank and product.type != blank
    assign type_query = product.type | url_encode
    assign crumb_title = product.type
    assign crumb_url = routes.search_url | append: '?q=' | append: type_query
  endif
-%}
{%- if format == 'html' -%}
  <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}">Home</a><span>/</span>
    {%- if crumb_url != blank -%}
      <a href="{{ crumb_url }}">{{ crumb_title }}</a><span>/</span>
    {%- endif -%}
    <span class="muted">{{ product.title | truncate: 60 }}</span>
  </nav>
{%- else -%}
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          "position": 1,
          "name": "Home",
          "item": {{ shop.url | json }}
        },
        {%- if crumb_url != blank -%}
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          "position": 2,
          "name": {{ crumb_title | json }},
          "item": {{ shop.url | append: crumb_url | json }}
        },
        {%- endif -%}
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          "position": {% if crumb_url != blank %}3{% else %}2{% endif %},
          "name": {{ product.title | json }},
          "item": {{ shop.url | append: product.url | json }}
        }
{%- endif -%}
